        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="2045" n="1894" xml:id="pg1894"/>

                <head>482. Memorandum from Read to Bundy, December 20<anchor n="1" xml:id="d482-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-12-20">December 20, 1963</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d482-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d482-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Wool Textiles</item>
                </list>
                <p>The attached memorandum provides information concerning United States imports of
                    wool textiles and quantitative limitations imposed by Italy and the United
                    Kingdom on wool textiles exported by Japan. This information was requested in a
                    letter to the Under Secretary from Mr. Feldman dated November 20, 1963.</p>
                <closer><signed>Benjamin H. Read</signed>
                    <affiliation>Executive Secretary</affiliation></closer>

                <pb facs="d482-4" n="4" type="facsimile" xml:id="d482-4"/>







